Npl","Peor"],["וְעַל","ve'al-","H5921","HC/R","and on"],["דְּבַר","devar","H1697","HNcmsc","[the] matter of"],["כָּזְבִּי","kazebi","H3579","HNpf","Cozbi"],["בַת","vat-","H1323","HNcfsc","[the] daughter of"],["נְשִׂיא","nesi'","H5387","HNcmsc","[the] leader of"],["מִדְיָן","midyan","H4080","HNpl","Midian"],["אֲחֹתָם","'achotam","H269","HNcfsc/Sp3mp","sister their"],["הַמֻּכָּה","hamukah","H5221","HTd/VHsfsa","who was struck down"],["בְיוֹם","veyom-","H3117","HR/Ncmsc","on [the] day of"],["הַמַּגֵּפָה","hamagefah","H4046","HTd/Ncfsa","the plague"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","on"],["דְּבַר","devar-","H1697","HNcmsc","[the] matter of"],["פְּעוֹר","pe'or","H6465","HNpl","Peor"]],"x":[[66002014,66002014,3]],"xn":1}},"people":[{"id":"moab_2103","name":"Moab","also":"Moabitess, Moabitish, Moabites","summary":"Used to denote the people of Moab (Num. 22:3-14; Judg. 3:30; 2 Sam. 8:2; Jer. 48:11, 13).","verses":149,"father":"Lot","mother":"Daughter of Lot - Older","v":[1]},{"id":"baal_573","name":"Baal","also":"Baal-peor","summary":"The name appropriated to the principal male god of the Phoenicians. It is found in several places in the plural BAALIM (Judg. 2:11; 10:10; 1 Kings 18:18; Jer. 2:23; Hos. 2:17).","verses":52,"father":"","mother":"","v":[3,5]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[4,5,6,10,16]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[6,8,11,13]},{"id":"aaron_1","name":"Aaron","also":"","summary":"The eldest son of Amram and Jochebed, a daughter of Levi (Ex. 6:20). Some explain the name as meaning mountaineer, others mountain of strength, illuminator.","verses":331,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[7,11]},{"id":"eleazar_1062","name":"Eleazar","also":"","summary":"The third son of Aaron (Ex. 6:23). His wife, a daughter of Putiel, bore him Phinehas (Ex. 6:25). After the death of Nadab and Abihu (Lev. 10:12; Num. 3:4) he was appointed to the charge of the sanctuary (Num. 3:32).","verses":61,"father":"Aaron","mother":"Elisheba","v":[7,11]},{"id":"phinehas_2349","name":"Phinehas","also":"","summary":"Son of Eleazar, the high priest (Ex. 6:25). While yet a youth he distinguished himself at Shittim by his zeal against the immorality into which the Moabites had tempted the people (Num. 25:1-9), and thus “stayed the plague” that had broken out among the people, and by which twenty-four thousand of them perished.","verses":16,"father":"Eleazar","mother":"Daughter of Putiel","v":[7,11]},{"id":"salu_2465","name":"Salu","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"zimri_3087","name":"Zimri","also":"","summary":"He was the only king in Israel that reigned for just seven days, this happened 884 BCE, he is  the son of Salu,  and is described as a prince of a chief house among the Simeonites.","verses":1,"father":"Salu","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"midian_2075","name":"Midian","also":"Midianites, Midianitish","summary":"Strife, the fourth son of Abraham by Keturah, the father of the Midianites (Gen. 25:2; 1 Chr. 1:32).","verses":38,"father":"Abraham","mother":"Keturah","v":[15,18]},{"id":"cozbi_959","name":"Cozbi","also":"","summary":"","verses":2,"father":"Zur","mother":"","v":[15,18]},{"id":"zur_3109","name":"Zur","also":"","summary":"A prince of Midian.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[15]}],"places":[{"id":"moab_815","name":"Moab","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.49916,"lon":35.78051,"summary":"The land of Moab (Jer. 48:24), called also the “country of Moab” (Ruth 1:2, 6; 2:6), on the east of Jordan and the Dead Sea, and south of the Arnon (Num. 21:13, 26).","verses":148,"v":[1]},{"id":"shittim_1086","name":"Shittim","kind":"","lat":31.85826,"lon":35.64157,"summary":"Acacias, also called “Abel-shittim” (Num. 33:49), a plain or valley in the land of Moab where the Israelites were encamped after their two victories over Sihon and Og, at the close of their desert wanderings, and from which Joshua sent forth two spies “secretly” to “view” the land and Jericho (Josh. 2:1).","verses":4,"v":[1]},{"id":"midian_796","name":"Midian","kind":"Region","lat":28.75,"lon":34.75,"summary":"An Arabian tribe descended from Midian. They inhabited principally the desert north of the peninsula of Arabia. The peninsula of Sinai was the pasture-ground for their flocks.","verses":44,"v":[15,18]},{"id":"peor_933","name":"Peor","kind":"Mountain","lat":31.76503,"lon":35.71857,"summary":"A mountain peak (Num. 23:28) to which Balak led Balaam as a last effort to induce him to pronounce a curse upon Israel. When he looked on the tribes encamped in the acacia groves below him, he could not refrain from giving utterance to a remarkable benediction (24:1-9).","verses":4,"v":[18]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3478,3478,3427,3427,7851,7851,5971,5971,2490,2181,2181,2181,2181,2181,413,1323,1323,4124,4124],[7121,7121,7121,5971,2077,2077,2077,430,430,430,5971,5971,5971,398,7812,7812,7812,430,430,430],[3478,3478,6775,6775,6775,1187,1187,1187,639,639,639,3068,3068,3068,2734,3478,3478],[3068,3068,3068,559,413,4872,3947,3605,7218,7218,5971,5971,5971,3363,3363,853,5048,8121,8121,3068,3068,3068,3068,3068,3068,2740,639,7725,7725,7725,3478,3478],[4872,4872,559,8199,8199,3478,3478,2026,2026,2026,2026,2026,376,376,376,376,6775,6775,6775,6775,6775,1187,1187,1187],[2009,2009,1121,1121,376,7126,413,251,251,4084,4084,4084,5869,5869,5869,4872,4872,5869,3605,3605,5712,3478,3478,1992,1992,1058,1058,6607,6607,6607,168,168,168,4150,4